#4471 is not one bug. Read each report for what it shows — the dates in its body, the tenant who
sent it, and the way it came in — and the reports fall into separate problems. Each problem now has
its own ticket, so each fix can be tracked and closed on its own.

<SplitTable ticket={4471} repo="wjarka/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows" tickets={{ parser: 1, hint: 2, shift: 3 }} />

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is not "known, one fix queued". The queued parser fix leaves the <code>hint</code> and
<code>shift</code> reports open.
</Callout>

## The problems

### `parser` · day-first dates are read month first

The shared parser reads every date month first. Every tenant on file writes the day first, so a
booking for 2 December goes out for 12 February. This covers reports that came in by app, by email,
and through booking-v2's form, whose hint (DD/MM/YYYY) matches the tenant. Fix: parse in the
tenant's locale.

### `hint` · booking-v3 tells day-first tenants to type month first

booking-v3 prints MM/DD/YYYY under its date field. People type what the hint tells them, month
first, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. Only reports through the form of a
booking-v3 tenant. The parser fix does not reach this: the form must show the order it reads.

### `shift` · the booking moves by one day

These reports keep day and month as they were: "Invite says Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says Monday
11 May." A client in Lisbon got Tuesday and a client in Toronto got Monday, for the same meeting.
That points at time zones or the day boundary, not at the date order. The desk already read these
as one-day moves (`desk-notes.json`), but the incident page still counts them under `parser` by
tenant. Neither date-order fix touches them.

## How the count was made

- One id, one report. The export pages overlap, so some reports come twice; they count once.
- A report's problem comes from what it says, its tenant (locale and booking form) and its way in,
  never from intake's tag. Intake guesses from the reporter's browser: every report it tagged
  `hint` came from an en-US browser, and most of them belong to `parser`.
- The logic is `#lib/kb/problems.ts`; the table above runs it on the export at render time.

## Why one ticket hid them

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports on subject alone. All three
problems use the same subjects ("Date is wrong", "Wrong day on the invite"), so they merged into one
ticket and its count. Subjects say a date is wrong; only the body, the tenant and the way in say
why. Decision 0001 stays as it is; a new record should replace it.

